  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Elections in the United States were held on November 3, 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384252488:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The article records that support for Medicare for All and a wealth tax points to an economic populist thread that extends beyond young Democrats.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384252488:230"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Democrats won Senate seats that Republicans previously held in Iowa, Ohio, South Carolina, Maine, Kansas, North Carolina and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384252488:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "There are 35 Senate races this year: Democrats have won 20, Republicans 13, and 2 are not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:the-senate-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:31Z",
      "text": "Democratic gains came in Iowa, North Carolina, Kansas, Maine, Ohio, South Carolina and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ia",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-nc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ks",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-me",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-oh-special",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-sc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-tx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "There are 36 governor's races this year, with 0 won by Democrats, 0 won by Republicans, and 36 not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The House stands at 254 Democratic seats and 162 Republican seats, with 19 still to be called, and 218 seats make a majority.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-infobox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:00:55Z",
      "text": "On the map, 53 districts changed party, and 20 are not yet called in the race tables.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:01:03Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the articles on Jon Ossoff (325,378), Gina Hinojosa (284,450) and 2026 United States Senate elections (170,346).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Jon_Ossoff:2026-11-05",
        "views:en:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-05",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_Senate_elections:2026-11-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:01:12Z",
      "text": "The English article drew 356,470 readers on 5 November 2026, about 14 times its usual daily level.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-05",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "The article is available in 11 languages, and after English the most readers were in Chinese, with 16,699.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-05",
        "views:zh:2026年美國選舉:2026-11-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:01:26Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not the same as a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:zh:2026年美國選舉:2026-11-05",
        "views:de:Wahlen_in_den_Vereinigten_Staaten_2026:2026-11-05",
        "views:fa:انتخابات_۲۰۲۶_ایالات_متحده_آمریکا:2026-11-05",
        "views:pt:Eleições_nos_Estados_Unidos_em_2026:2026-11-05",
        "views:fr:Élections_de_2026_aux_États-Unis:2026-11-05",
        "views:it:Elezioni_parlamentari_negli_Stati_Uniti_d'America_del_2026:2026-11-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-05T00:01:36Z",
      "text": "The sources are Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageview counts and Wikidata, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
